oindent The start and end nodes are the same, but the multiplicative factors are different as long as $k
e m$. This happens because the mid-step is different ($\Phi_{n-k}$ for the first case and $\Phi_{n-m}$ for the second). In particular,  egin{eqnarray} \left[ \Delta_{-mA}, \Delta_{-kA} ight] \Phi_n &=& S_{-m}\, S_{-k} \left( m-k ight) \left(n-m-kight) \Phi_{n-m-k} = 
