Let us next write a few examples of discontinuities one may compute (we choose them as they will be useful in what follows). These should not be too hard to obtain, and we leave it as an exercise for the reader to prove them.  egin{itemize} \item The Stokes discontinuity along the positive real line is unchanged in this new chain, as there are no new forward motions. It is actually straightforward to find a general expression for all sectors, as  egin{eqnarray} {\mathrm{Disc}}_{0} \Phi_{(n,0)} (x) &=& - \sum_{k=1}^{+\infty}  inom{n+k}{n}\, S_1^k\, {\mathrm{e}}^{- rac{kA}{x}}\, \Phi_{(n+k,0)} (x) \ &=& \sum_{k=1}^{+\infty} \mathsf{S}_{n	o n+k}\, {\mathrm{e}}^{- rac{kA}{x}}\, \Phi_{(n+k,0)} (x). 
onumber \end{eqnarray} \item The Stokes discontinuities along the negative real line will now have contributions from paths ending on the new node $\Phi_{(0,1)} = F_0^{(0,1)}$. A few examples are:  egin{eqnarray} {\mathrm{Disc}}_{\pi} \Phi_{(1,0)}(x) &=& - \widetilde{S}_{-1}\, {\mathrm{e}}^{ rac{A}{x}}\, \Phi_{(0,1)} = \widetilde{\mathsf{S}}_{1	o0}\, {\mathrm{e}}^{ rac{A}{x}}\, \Phi_{(0,1)}, \ {\mathrm{Disc}}_{\pi} \Phi_{(2,0)}(x) &=& - S_{-1}\, {\mathrm{e}}^{ rac{A}{x}}\, \Phi_{(1,0)}(x) - \left( \widetilde{S}_{-2} +  rac{1}{2!} S_{-1} \widetilde{S}_{-1} ight) {\mathrm{e}}^{ rac{2A}{x}}\, \Phi_{(0,1)} \ &=& \mathsf{S}_{2	o1}\, {\mathrm{e}}^{ rac{A}{x}}\, \Phi_{(1,0)}(x) + \widetilde{\mathsf{S}}_{2	o0}\, {\mathrm{e}}^{ rac{2A}{x}}\, \Phi_{(0,1)}, 
